# Ni - Ugur interatomic potential, RECOMMENDED for molecular dynamics, re-cut, switched
#
# pair_style ugur
# pair_coeff * * Ni_recut.ugur Ni
#
# Truncation: switched from 0.85 of each cutoff to the cutoff, quintic, C2 - energy is conserved in MD.  RECOMMENDED for molecular dynamics on Ni, in place of Ni_taper.ugur, which still ships.  It passes every screen of the rule - stable, ground state, MD screen; expansion > 0; C11 not stiffening between the lowest MD temperature and 300 K; 300 K elastic error and measured dispersion no more than 2 points worse than the switched set - which standalone/recommend_recut.py applies to every element that has a re-cut, not by hand
# MD: structure screened - holds its shape at 600 K (300 K, as equipartition requires).  This tested the SHAPE, not energy conservation; for that see the truncation line above.
#
# Lattice stability: screened on the 8^3 and 9^3 meshes AND along the
# symmetry path; no imaginary modes.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Measured dispersion: 12.1 % against 13.4 % for the published switched
# arm - better.
# Over the 21 accepted re-cut records: thermal expansion error 30.7 % -> 25.6 %
# median, 10 better and 10 worse; elastic constants near 300 K against the
# room-temperature values 5.2 % -> 3.4 % median, 11 better and 10 worse.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Ni at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
Ni Ni Ni 2.1182149991454482 0.32378552281483369 0.86213326143543001 3.143437322585855 1.1998375453629655 -0.44541645601699609 2.1077532411009305 8.4483489042144857 3.7377664453520905 0.84999999999999998 0 0
